# Audio checks (audio work): the start-up and the title screen (with whatever plays there), the map zoom-out, the
# city with the radio, then a drive. Run it with --intro normal and real-time updates (no --fixed-dt: the sound
# is real time, a timedemo would run the game's clock ahead of it). Segments (marks): title, map_zoom, free_roam,
# drive, end. The marks are in game.log with their time, which the analysis uses to say where in the run a gap or
# a click was (launcher/dev/audio/audio_analyze.py).
wait 8s
mark title
# Stay on the title screen for the attract movie and the music before leaving it.
wait 37s
press_until start left_title every=2s timeout=90s
mark map_zoom
wait_until roam 180s
mark free_roam
# The radio plays in the car at the spawn point.
wait 25s
mark drive
# Out of the car park and along the street, as drive-spawn.pad, then straight on.
trigger rt 1 50f
trigger rt 0.6
stick lx 1 40f
trigger rt 1
wait 70s
release all
mark end
